cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or cite the KNOBE Protocol, cite it as below."
title: "KNOBE Protocol v1: A Context Protocol for Responsible Knowledge Movement"
authors:
  - family-names: Kyle
    given-names: David
    affiliation: "University of California, Davis"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-06-28
url: "https://knobe.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/KnobeOne/knobe-protocol"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.21298913"
    description: "Zenodo archive of the KNOBE Protocol v1 white paper"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  An open, plain-text protocol for knowledge objects that keep their context
  when they move. A KNOBE is a single markdown file carrying its readable
  content together with a machine-legible, hash-sealed record of attribution,
  transformation history, fidelity limits, and use conditions.
keywords:
  - provenance
  - knowledge-objects
  - open-specification
  - mcp
  - integrity
